# Positivus Landing Page

A digital marketing agency landing page built with HTML and CSS.

## About the Project

This project is a landing page inspired by the Positivus digital marketing agency design. The goal is to practice front-end development by building a multi-section website and exploring my own visual design decisions.

## Built With

- HTML5
- CSS3
- Flexbox
- CSS Grid
- Google Fonts — Space Grotesk
- SVG assets

## Sections

- Hero Section
- Services — six service cards
- Contact Us
- Case Studies

## Features

- Custom visual styling inspired by the Positivus design
- Grid layout for service cards
- Flexbox for component alignment
- SVG illustrations and company logos
- Space Grotesk typography

## Getting Started

1. Clone this repository.
2. Open the project folder in Visual Studio Code.
3. Open `index.html` in a browser, or use the Live Server extension.

## Project Status

In progress. Responsive improvements, visual refinements, and further development are planned.

## What I Learned

- Structuring a landing page with semantic HTML
- Using CSS Flexbox and Grid
- Organizing reusable CSS classes
- Integrating Google Fonts and SVG assets
- Managing project progress with Git and GitHub

